d 'PROJECTBACKUP': module to zip up a project folder, subfolders included, in native Stata
d
d  projectbackup archives a folder and everything under it into a
d single .zip using only Stata's own zipfile command and Mata -- no
d tar, 7-Zip, or PowerShell, so it behaves identically on macOS,
d Windows, and Linux and works where you cannot run external
d programs. It is built for the everyday "snapshot my project"
d habit: point it at a folder and it writes a (optionally dated)
d zip into an _archive subfolder, and can keep a running Markdown
d log of every backup. Before writing it walks the tree and warns
d about oversized folders, too many files, and paths too deep for
d Windows to extract -- with a dryrun that measures without
d writing. Options: archive(), prefix(), timestamp, label(),
d exclude(), nodotfiles, toc, note(), manifest, keep(), removeall,
d dryrun, force, and a zippy option that also writes a Stata
d Journal .zippy copy. projectbackup [folder] [, timestamp toc
d exclude() keep() dryrun ...] 
d
d KW: backup; archive; zip; zipfile; project; reproducibility; Stata Journal
d
d Requires: Stata version 14
d
d Distribution-Date: 20260730
d
d Author: Eric A. Booth, Texas 2036
d Support: email eric.a.booth@@gmail.com
d
f projectbackup.ado
f projectbackup.sthlp
